16 0 obj
<<
/A 56 0 R
/Alt (PRISMA flow diagram detailing the selection process for records on "presence" and "virtual reality." Identification yields 21,482 records; 4,691 are removed before screening, leaving 16,791 screened. From these, 10,155 are excluded for not relating to "sense of presence in VR," resulting in 6,636 eligible records. No records are excluded at the eligibility stage, with all 6,636 included for analysis using Biblioshiny and VOSviewer.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 38 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
17 0 obj
<<
/A 56 0 R
/Alt (Infographic displaying research data: Timespan 1992-2024, 2,542 sources, 6,636 documents, 20,041 authors, 555 single-authored documents, 15.37% international co-authorship, 4.47 co-authors per document, 10,913 author keywords, 219,349 references, 7.75 average document age, and 24.11 average citations per document. Annual growth rate 14.54%.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 39 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
18 0 obj
<<
/A 56 0 R
/Alt (Line graph depicting annual scientific production from 1992 to 2024, showing a general increasing trend. The number of articles gradually rises from near zero in 1992 approaching 200 by 1995. Output accelerates after 1995 to reach over 800 in 2023.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 40 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
19 0 obj
<<
/A 56 0 R
/Alt (Three-field Sankey diagram tracing interactions between author country on the left, author name in the middle, and cited references by name on the right. Node size is proportional to the strength of relationships between columns. Countries featured include Italy, Spain, the UK, Korea, Germany, and Portugal. International collaborations are present, but the strongest collaborations occur between geographically co-located researchers. Citations show a high occurrence of self-referencing.)
/K 1
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 40 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
20 0 obj
<<
/A 56 0 R
/Alt (Bar chart titled "Most Relevant Sources" displaying the number of documents from various academic sources. "Lecture Notes in Computer Science" leads with 297 documents, followed by "Presence-Teleoperators and Virtual Environments" with 261 documents. Other sources have fewer than 154 documents. The x-axis represents the number of documents, ranging from 0 to 300, and the y-axis lists the source names. A "Bibliometrix" logo is at the bottom right.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 41 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
21 0 obj
<<
/A 56 0 R
/Alt (Bubble chart titled "Authors' Production over Time," comparing authors' article production by year from 1993 to 2023. Each row represents an author, with bubble size indicating the number of articles and shade representing citations.)
/K 1
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 41 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
