<<
/A 56 0 R
/Alt (Co-citation network map visualising links between academic papers based on the degree to which references are cited within the same document. Nodes represent a single reference, colour-coded by clusters, with connecting lines indicating link strength. Larger nodes signify link strength and show higher centrality or influence within the network.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 45 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
26 0 obj
<<
/A 56 0 R
/Alt (Bibliographic coupling network diagram depicting clusters of interconnected nodes based on the extent to which authors have shared references in their bibliography. Nodes represent a single author, the size of the node is proportional to their link strength in the network.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 47 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
27 0 obj
<<
/A 56 0 R
/Alt (Bibliographic coupling network diagram depicting clusters of interconnected nodes based on the extent to which authors have shared references in their bibliography. The colour overlay based on the average publication year, ranging from blue 2010 to yellow 2020, indicates authors with a long history of research \(blue\) and emerging authors \(yellow\). Nodes represent a single author, the size of the node is proportional to their link strength in the network.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 48 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
